          <div class="section-label">Complete Buyer's Guide</div>
          <h2 id="guide-heading">Everything You Need to Know About Buying a Home in Torrance, CA</h2>
          <p>Torrance is one of the most underappreciated cities in the South Bay for buyers who have done their homework. With five distinct zip codes, a school district that ranks in the top 15–20% statewide, a city median around $1.1 million, and price points ranging from $600K condos in 90502 to $2M+ single-family homes in 90505, Torrance has a path for buyers across a genuinely wide range of financial profiles.</p>
          <h3 id="which-zip">Which Zip Code Is Right for You?</h3>
          <p>The first question every Torrance buyer needs to answer is which zip code matches their priorities. Here is a quick framework:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>90502 (North Torrance):</strong> Best entry point into the market. FHA loans available. Freeway access. Long-term upside.</li>
            <li><strong>90501 (Old Torrance):</strong> Historic character and walkability. Conventional financing. Mid-$900Ks median.</li>
            <li><strong>90504 (Northwest Torrance):</strong> Practical mid-market value. Conventional financing. Torrance USD schools.</li>
            <li><strong>90503 (West Torrance):</strong> Most competitive zip. Best schools. Multiple offers common. Conventional and jumbo.</li>
            <li><strong>90505 (South Torrance):</strong> Premium PV-adjacent pricing. South High feeder. Jumbo financing standard.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="financing-torrance">Financing in Torrance — Which Programs Apply</h3>
          <p>The 2025 conforming loan limit in LA County is $1,209,750. In Torrance, this means:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>FHA loans apply in 90502 and parts of 90501 and 90504 where purchase prices fall within FHA program limits.</li>
            <li>Conventional high-balance loans cover the $900K–$1.2M range that characterizes much of 90501, 90503, and 90504.</li>
            <li>Jumbo loans are required for most West Torrance (90503) single-family homes above $1.2M and nearly all South Torrance (90505) purchases.</li>
            <li>Bank statement loans are available for self-employed buyers who cannot fully document qualifying income on tax returns.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="schools-torrance">Torrance USD and School Quality</h3>
          <p>Torrance Unified School District ranks in the top 15–20% of California public school districts and is a primary driver of home values across all five zip codes. North High, South High, and West High all serve different zip codes within the district, with South High in 90505 typically ranking highest among the three. Understanding which high school serves a specific neighborhood — and how that affects pricing — is an important part of the buyer conversation in Torrance.</p>
          <h3 id="next-steps-torrance">Your Next Step</h3>
          <p>Whether you're targeting a first home in North Torrance, a family upgrade in West Torrance, or a South Torrance premium purchase near PV — let's figure out the right financing path. Call me at (310) 594-5362 or fill out the form below. Free, 20 minutes, honest answers.</p>
